    <dashboard name='What&apos;s new'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/AutoCompperformance/Whatsnew?rev=' id='Whatsnew' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/AutoCompperformance' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='text-align' id='dash-text_1' value='left' />
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_1' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='parameter-ctrl'>
          <format attr='background-color' value='#d00920' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='parameter-ctrl-title'>
          <format attr='text-align' value='center' />
          <format attr='color' value='#ffffff' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='1200' maxwidth='1400' minheight='1200' minwidth='1400' preset-index='17' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98666' id='1' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='667'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontsize='12'>This dashboard replaces the Autocomp Impact dashboard (</run>
              <run auto-url='true' fontsize='12' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/#/site/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/10373/views&amp;quot;'>https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/#/site/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/10373/views</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>). </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>Whats&apos;s new:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- The underlying data is available @ </run>
              <run fontcolor='#e01e5a' fontname='Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,Courier New,monospace' fontsize='11'>`fulfillment-dwh-production.curated_data_shared_gcc_service.autocomp_events` </run>
              <run fontsize='12'>and</run>
              <run fontcolor='#e01e5a' fontname='Monaco,Menlo,Consolas,Courier New,monospace' fontsize='11'> `fulfillment-dwh-production.curated_data_shared_gcc_service.autocomp_events_enriched` </run>
              <run fontsize='12'>(details: </run>
              <run auto-url='true' fontsize='12' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://deliveryhero.slack.com/archives/CDMBP1PK7/p1617095920044500&amp;quot;'>https://deliveryhero.slack.com/archives/CDMBP1PK7/p1617095920044500</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>)</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- The </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>budget section</run>
              <run fontsize='12'> has been spun out into a separate dashboard (</run>
              <run auto-url='true' fontsize='12' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/#/site/GlobalStandardReporting/views/AutoCompBudget/BudgetDashboard&amp;quot;'>https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/#/site/GlobalStandardReporting/views/AutoCompBudget/BudgetDashboard</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- With this revamp, we have shifted focus towards ROI metrics - Incremental GMV per cost supercedes iCPO (iCPO is still available in </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>Experiments summary</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>). More details on metrics are available in the glossary.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>Top line</run>
              <run fontsize='12'> now has more level of detail (new funnel metrics). Dimension parameters allow you to drill into segments of your choice.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>Experiment summary</run>
              <run fontsize='12'> gives a summary of each experiment&apos;s performance.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>Experiment details</run>
              <run fontsize='12' italic='true'>Æ </run>
              <run fontsize='12'>gives a break-down of the experiment&apos;s performance into variant groups and over time. In case of visible experimentation issues in the time-series, adjust your time-frame accordingly and the aggregates at the top will mirror the selected time-frame. In case of several treatment groups, you can split or combine them via a parameter. We show a 95% confidence interval for the reorder rate of each variant.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>Graph explorer </run>
              <run fontsize='12'>allows you to plot standard metrics by standard dimensions over time.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- The complexity of </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>decision-policy </run>
              <run fontsize='12'>and </run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>action-type </run>
              <run fontsize='12'>is now opaque. For decision-policy performance, please refer to your experiment details. Action-type information is now encoded via</run>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='12'> % Compensation rate.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>- Cohort time-frame is now fixed to seven days (arbitrary time-frames are available in the underlying data).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='12'>Feel free to ping in #dh-gst-bi with any questions/issues.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
